From 815dedd031ddec0db846d2e6d06d40d5057e1aee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri John Ledkov <dimitri.ledkov@chainguard.dev>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:41:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Gate every legacy algorithm behind a new
 "enable-legacy-allowed" switch

Add a provider parameter "enable-legacy-allowed", defaulting to 0.  While
it is off, the provider's query callback answers every operation with an
empty algorithm list, so nothing from this module can be fetched -- the
same outcome as "activate = 0" -- but the provider is still loaded,
activated and registered with the core: OSSL_PROVIDER_available() reports
it, "openssl list -providers" shows it as active, and its parameters can
be queried.  Set it with "enable-legacy-allowed = 1" in the provider's
configuration section, OSSL_PROVIDER_add_conf_parameter(), or
-provparam legacy:enable-legacy-allowed=1 on the command line.

The value is read the same way as "enable-des", through the core's
get_params upcall with ossl_prov_ctx_get_bool_param(), and is checked
before the per-operation switch, so "enable-des" has no effect unless the
provider as a whole is enabled.  Because the core remembers which
operations it has already asked a provider about, both parameters must be
set before the first fetch; this is now noted in the source and README.

The test configurations that activate the legacy provider --
test/legacy.cnf, test/default-and-legacy.cnf and the 90-test_includes
data file -- set the parameter, so the test suite continues to see the
full algorithm set.  Those with "activate = false" are unchanged.

Verified with a no-asm no-quic no-secure-memory build: legacy.so still
depends only on libc and exports only OSSL_provider_init; "openssl list"
shows no legacy algorithms by default, seven with the switch, nine with
enable-des as well, and none with enable-des alone; the provider stays
listed as active in the off state; an MD5 fetch with -propquery
provider=legacy succeeds with the switch and fails without it; evp_test on
evpciph_rc4.txt passes under the updated test/legacy.cnf and fails rather
than skipping when the switch line is removed; and conf_include_test
-providers passes.

README-LEGACY-FREESTANDING.md documents the parameter, the updated
"openssl list" and known-answer command lines, and the first-fetch caveat.

